  "content": {
    "id": "p41-q49-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "49",
    "prompt": "The sum of 12 terms of an arithmetic series is 186 and the 20th term is 83. Find the sum of 40 terms of the series.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$3420$",
      "worked": "$S_{12}=186$, $a_{20}=83$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S_{12}&=\\frac{12}{2}[2a+11d]=186\\\\6(2a+11d)&=186\\\\2a+11d&=31\\qquad(1)\\\\a_{20}=a+19d&=83\\qquad(2)\\end{align*}$$\n\nFrom (2):\n\n$$a=83-19d.$$\n\nSubstitute into (1):\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2(83-19d)+11d&=31\\\\166-38d+11d&=31\\\\-27d&=-135\\\\d&=5\\end{align*}$$\n\nFrom (2):\n\n$$a=83-95=-12.$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S_{40}&=\\frac{40}{2}[2(-12)+39(5)]\\\\S_{40}&=3420\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
